				<div class="mw-body-content">
					<div id="contentSub"><p></p></div><div id="mw-content-text" class="mw-body-content mw-content-ltr" lang="en" dir="ltr"><div class="mw-parser-output"><div class="messagebox" style="background-color: #f9f6b7; border: 1px solid #c4c295; color: black; padding: 5px; margin: 1ex 0; min-height: 35px; padding-left: 45px;">
<div style="float: left; margin-left: -40px;"><a href="https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/File:Warning.png" class="image"><img alt="Warning.png" src="https://fedoraproject.org/w/uploads/thumb/c/cb/Warning.png/35px-Warning.png" decoding="async" width="35" height="35"></a></div>
<div>This page is outdated and needs to be verified against current releases of Fedora.</div>
</div>
<p>Setting up a root password is a mandatory part of a Fedora installation. If you forget or otherwise lose your root password, there are procedures to reset it.
</p>
<ul><li>If you have set a password for your boot loader, refer to <a href="https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/How_to_reset_a_root_password#using-installation-cd-dvd"> this section</a>.</li>
<li>If you want to reset the boot loader password, refer to <a href="https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Reset_Bootloader_Password" title="Reset Bootloader Password"> these instructions</a>.</li>
<li>If none of these scenarios apply to you, proceed to <a href="https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/How_to_reset_a_root_password#Entering_Rescue_Mode"> the next section</a>.</li></ul>
<p>Fedora uses <i>targets</i> to determine the services being run when you start your system. Run level 1 can be used as a rescue mode. Booting Linux under run level 1, which is also called <i>single user mode</i>, will display a root prompt on bootup, from which you can reset the root password.
</p>
<div id="toc" class="toc" role="navigation" aria-labelledby="mw-toc-heading"><input type="checkbox" role="button" id="toctogglecheckbox" class="toctogglecheckbox" style="display:none"><div class="toctitle" lang="en" dir="ltr"><h2 id="mw-toc-heading">Contents</h2><span class="toctogglespan"><label class="toctogglelabel" for="toctogglecheckbox"></label></span></div>
<ul>
<li class="toclevel-1 tocsection-1"><a href="https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/How_to_reset_a_root_password#Entering_Rescue_Mode"><span class="tocnumber">1</span> <span class="toctext">Entering Rescue Mode</span></a>
